    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e969255c-4607-54cb-b56b-c47b0303893d",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\text{det}(X)$, if\n$X=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{aligned}].$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(X) & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5\\cdot 3-8\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =15-(-48) \\\\  & =63\\end{aligned}\n$$",
